sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task; DECISIONS R1 + round 2 websocket.sync (no polling step, the Gateway closes the task from Reverb's own reports, no run).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: websocket:sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant N as Reverb<br/>on websocket Node
  CLI->>GW: websocket:sync<br/>--wait=60 --operation-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit websocket:sync --wait=60`
  %%> - syntax: `[--wait=SECONDS] [--operation-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - `--wait`: how long the CLI follows the task, 0 to 3600 seconds; default 60
  %%> - optionally an operation key, to retry the same sync
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - waits until every serving Reverb process has applied the current registry, without a restart
  Note over GW: Pin current registry<br/>revision 18 · R1, no run
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a Node has the `websocket` role
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - records task #5125 for the current registry revision 18
  %%> - a pending app change does not block it, and separate syncs do not replace each other
  %%> Why no Swamp run:
  %%> - nothing has to be done on a Node; Reverb pulls and reports itself (R1)
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5125
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show` until `--wait` ends
  loop each Reverb reconcile, 30 s
    N->>GW: Pull the registry<br/>full snapshot
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - every Reverb process fetches the full snapshot on its own 30-second reconcile
    %%> - an unchanged revision answers `304`
    N->>GW: Report applied revision<br/>per process and boot
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each process reports the revision it applied, with its boot identity
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a report from an old boot cannot confirm a replacement process
  end
  alt every process applied 18
    Note over GW: Close the task<br/>succeeded · backend applied
    %%> Result:
    %%> - every serving Reverb process runs revision 18 or later with the same apps
    %%> - task #5125 succeeds
  else stale, superseded, timeout
    Note over GW: Close the task, failed<br/>websocket.registry_pending
    %%> When:
    %%> - a serving process is stale or missing after 5 minutes
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5125 fails; the registry stays as saved
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after the fix
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal or --wait
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5125
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended or `--wait` has passed
    %%> When `--wait` passes first:
    %%> - the CLI exits non-zero; the task keeps waiting, and nothing is undone
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
